Feature: spa-named-route-params (RETROACTIVE — commit e19f2cd, logged after the
changelog/ convention was introduced in 478c817)
Target module: SPAEngine

- ;name and ;name:regex pattern segments capture route params by name (legacy :regex
  stays positional), with regex validation per segment.
- routeProperties.data now passed as the last argument to bootCallback,
  clickLoadCallbacks, historyCallbacks and the clickLoadCallback fallback.
- history.pushState uses the actual requested route (e.g /user/7) instead of the
  configured path literal, so dynamic URLs survive refresh/bookmark.

Affected projects: any consumer of vUX-spaEngine.js using dynamic routes; existing
positional :regex patterns keep working unchanged.
